From 91ff285c0ac3e8b86c6ade6b4dde9375eae4b418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:28:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] managed worker: adopt only its own session's
 orphaned background jobs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Kanban managed worker's startup recover_from_checkpoint() adopted every
orphan on the host. On hermes-hub 2026-11-13 the always-on Desktop backend
@9148 rolled over at 00:10:01 while Desktop chat 20261112_002413_39be4c's
persist_on_release + notify_on_complete job proc_70810e2dae05 ran. A Kanban
worker (pid 49656, session local-0581b9b9…, 00:10:14-00:15:47) started 17 s
later and adopted the job. Its writer stamp fenced the successor backend's
30 s keeper, so process_manage returned not_found at 00:11:38. Its log reader
collected the exit at 00:15:02 (receipt mtime 00:15) into a completion queue
nobody reads, and the chat never got its notice.

recover_from_checkpoint gains session_keys=. The worker passes its route and
session id (F24's intent: "a previous admission of this session"), and every
other entry stays untouched for its owner's recovery. Gateway and Desktop
recovery are unchanged.

Regression: tests/gateway/test_managed_worker_checkpoint_scope.py drives the
real managed-worker execute and recovery against a Desktop orphan plus an
orphan of the worker's own session. RED before the fix: the worker adopts
proc_desktop00001, and session_keys is a TypeError.
